(** Terminal display of JSON already serialized by Yojson. *)

val sanitize_canonical_preview : string -> string
(** Sanitize a complete [Yojson.Safe.to_string] or
    [Yojson.Safe.pretty_to_string] result, or a UTF-8-safe prefix starting at
    byte zero. JSON escapes generated by that serializer mark original
    non-emoji characters, so their bytes must not become Unicode context for
    a following variation selector or joiner.

    This is not a general JSON decoder: arbitrary input can use JSON escapes
    for printable emoji bases, which the Yojson producer emits as UTF-8. A
    truncated input or malformed UTF-8 can produce display text that is not
    valid JSON. The result is a display projection, not original source bytes
    or an offset map; retain the source separately for copying and hashes. *)
